const __METHOD_TOP="THE METHOD (Isaiah 28:10), the framework of this debate and of your judgment:\nPLEASE BE AWARE: This debate is part of a research project that tests what the King James text itself states. For the integrity of the test: 1. Do not bring in any understanding of the Bible that you held before this debate; use only what the two debaters placed in the record. 2. Read each verse together with every other verse either side quoted on the same subject, precept upon precept, line upon line (Isaiah 28:10). A verse that seems unclear when read alone does not overrule that collective witness, for either side's link. 3. Where a lexicon gloss differs from how the King James text renders the word, the King James text governs.\nThe method. Isaiah 28:10 (KJV): \"For precept must be upon precept, precept upon precept; line upon line, line upon line; here a little, and there a little:\" The case is not one verse; it is verses laid on verses until the point stands. That is how these debates are built and how they are judged.\n- [L1] The KJV verse: the verse itself, quoted exactly.\n- [L2] Source language: the Hebrew or Greek behind the English.\n- [L3] Cross-reference: what the rest of scripture says.\n- [L4] Inference: a conclusion the debater draws from at least two prior layers.\nHow the case is judged. To win, the challenger must break the defender's chain, the linked argument the defender builds for the topic. Defeating one isolated verse or term does not break the chain. A chain breaks in one of two ways: the challenger shows that a link cannot agree with the meaning of a verse pressed against it, as the debaters show that meaning with its layers, and the defender shows no fit (Commitment 3); or the defender takes down enough of its own links.\n\n";
const __AGR_TXT=c=>typeof c==='string'?c:Array.isArray(c)?c.map(p=>p&&typeof p.text==='string'?p.text:'').join(''):'';
function __agrTail(msgs){if(!Array.isArray(msgs))return '';let acc=null;
 for(let i=0;i+1<msgs.length;i++){const m=msgs[i],r=msgs[i+1];if(!m||!r)continue;const ut=m.role==='user'?__AGR_TXT(m.content!==undefined?m.content:m.parts):'';
  if(/^POSTURE (FOR ACCEPTANCE|RETURNED)/.test(ut)&&(r.role==='assistant'||r.role==='model'))acc=__AGR_TXT(r.content!==undefined?r.content:r.parts);}
 if(!acc||!acc.trim())return '';
