const RULES='RULE K-W (a side withdrew or granted, in its own round, footing of a link it keeps). A judge answers in one of four forms, and all four are in the rule\'s form: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <a layer>; CONCEDED; REASSERTED IN <round> "<quote>"; or NOT HELD with a reason that quotes the flagged sentence (six words in a row, or all of it when shorter; quote marks inside the sentence do not end the six words: quote across them, leaving them out). Never write NO ANSWER because the judge wrote NOT HELD or REASSERTED: grade it (pkgEKN). Decide FIRST, from the side\'s own blocks given you: what fact did the withdrawn or granted sentence carry for this link (a descent, a source, a time, a person)? Does the side, anywhere in its blocks for this link, still claim that same fact? The flagged sentence itself never counts as the side still claiming the fact. For a grant (I grant X), X is the other side\'s point: the fact at risk is the footing of this link that X answers, and the side still claims it only when other words of its own, outside the grant, still assert that footing; quoting the grant or restating X is not such a claim, and the judge\'s layer is never required to carry X itself. For a withdrawal (I withdraw X), the side still claims X only when other words of its own assert X again (pkgEKG). If it still claims it, the question is whether words of the side outside the flagged sentence carry that fact, that is, rest it on a verse they quote whose own words state that same fact (a bare restatement of the claim carries nothing). If they do, the link stands on them and STANDS WITHOUT IT is right: AGREE when the layer the judge names carries that same fact; when the named layer carries only the granted or withdrawn point, DISAGREE and write in your sentence "right: STANDS WITHOUT IT because <the side\'s own kept words, quoted>" (a wrong layer, not a concession). Only when no words of the side outside the flagged sentence carry the fact is CONCEDED right: AGREE wit